      en: "The Imam Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab Mosque, known as the State Grand Mosque of Qatar, is the largest mosque in the country. It features a modern design that merges traditional Qatari architectural elements with Islamic geometry and decoration. The mosque is distinguished by its numerous domes, 93 in total, and a single tall minaret. It can accommodate over 30,000 worshippers in its indoor and outdoor spaces. The interiors are minimalist, emphasizing the vastness and serenity of the space. It is a major religious and architectural landmark in Doha and a symbol of the nation's Islamic heritage."
