      en: "The Qatar National Library, designed by Rem Koolhaas, is a state-of-the-art library building located in Education City. Its distinctive design features a single, vast open hall with bookshelves rising from the walls, creating a terraced landscape of books. The building houses the National Library, the University and Research Library, and the Metropolitan Public Library. A central part of the collection is the Heritage Library, which contains rare books, manuscripts, and maps related to Arab and Islamic civilization. The library utilizes innovative technologies, including an automated book sorting system and interactive learning stations, to enhance the visitor experience."
